Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/aspeed: match AST2600 CNTFRQ to the emulated counter

The ARM generic timer uses integer nanosecond periods and caps its counter
at 1 GHz. Advertising 1.125 GHz makes Linux time advance at 8/9 speed.
Use the exactly representable 1 GHz rate for the Lenovo runtime build.
This requires a cold boot; do not apply to a running guest or old snapshot.

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
--- a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
+++ b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600.c
@@ -399,2 +399,3 @@
-        object_property_set_int(OBJECT(&a->cpu[i]), "cntfrq", 1125000000,
+        /* Match the generic timer's maximum effective rate (1 ns/tick). */
+        object_property_set_int(OBJECT(&a->cpu[i]), "cntfrq", 1000000000,
                                 &error_abort);
